{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '35,55p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '895,925p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '390,420p' bb.edn && cat .cljstyle\"","aggregated_output":"#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n\nThis ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\n\n## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n\nA single missing bracket can silently break an entire file. The compiler may still succeed, with subsequent forms nesting inside the broken one.\n\n1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\n   ```sh\n   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\n   ```\n\n2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\n   Do NOT try to eyeball-count brackets. Track a stack of `(char, line, col)` for every opener. Handle: string literals, escaped chars, and `;;` line comments.\n\n3. **Fix one bracket at a time, re-run checker after each fix**:\n   Common patterns:\n   - Hiccup vector missing `]` causes siblings to become extra arguments.\n   - `defn`/`let` missing `)` causes subsequent top-level forms to nest inside.\n   - Both can coexist while total bracket count is zero-sum.\n\n4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\n\n  ;; Subsystem tests (src/dev/affected.clj): canonical subsystems defined\n  ;; in src/dev/subsystems.edn. Positional arguments name subsystems; flags\n  ;; pass through (--lane L, --list, --slow).\n  test:sub {:doc \"Subsystem tests, three lanes in parallel: bb test:sub <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n            :depends [check:node-discovery]\n            :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \"--\")))\n                                                 *command-line-args*)\n                        sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\"--subsystem\" s]) subs)]\n                    (System/exit\n                      (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                    \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                    (concat sub-args flags)))))}\n\n  test:sub:clj {:doc \"JVM lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:clj <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n                :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \"--\")))\n                                                     *command-line-args*)\n                            sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\"--subsystem\" s]) subs)]\n                        (System/exit\n                          (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                        \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                        \"--lane\" \"clj\"\n                                        (concat sub-args flags)))))}\n\n  test:sub:cljs {:doc \"Node lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n                 :depends [check:node-discovery]\n                 :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \"--\")))\n                                                      *command-line-args*)\n                             sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\"--subsystem\" s]) subs)]\n                         (System/exit\n                           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n;; :namespaces is disabled project-wide. It rewrites ns forms, which is\n;; unsafe on this multi-platform codebase in two distinct ways:\n;; 1. ClojureDart uses string-prefixed :import forms (e.g.\n;;    (:import [\"dart:core\" BigInt DateTime])); the rule rewrites these\n;;    into JVM-style forms, which the cljd compiler then fails to resolve.\n;; 2. .cljc files that guard a JVM-only :import/:require clause with\n;;    #?(:cljd nil :clj ...) rely on :cljd appearing FIRST (the cljd\n;;    host-eval pass also matches :clj, so first-match-wins order is\n;;    load-bearing — see the reader-conditional trap in project memory).\n;;    The rule reorders reader-conditional branches alphabetically\n;;    (:clj before :cljd), silently re-breaking the guard on every\n;;    `cljstyle fix` — this bit dao.jing.dht.node.cljc and cost a lost\n;;    commit before being traced back here.\n{:files {:extensions #{\"blog\" \"chp\" \"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljd\" \"cljs\" \"edn\" \"jolt\"},\n         :ignore #{\".cpcache\" \".git\" \".shadow-cljs\" \"node_modules\" \"target\"}},\n :rules {:blank-lines {:enabled? true, :max-consecutive 2},\n         :eof-newline {:enabled? true},\n         :indentation {:enabled? true},\n         :namespaces {:enabled? false},\n         :whitespace\n           {:enabled? true, :insert-missing? true, :remove-trailing? true}}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
